From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1ma <hello@1ma.ai>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:00:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1ma: bb's cloud plugins are not shipped

1ma does not ship bb's cloud services, which send data to getbb.app, until
1ma runs its own. BB_CLOUD_PLUGIN_NAMES in @bb/domain lists bb-account,
bb-ai, connect and connect-next; the server and the desktop app both read
it.

Server: the plugins stay in BUNDLED_PLUGINS, because bb's catalog generator
needs an entry for each item there, but SHIPPED_PLUGINS and the bundled
registrations leave them out. On an existing install bb's orphan cleanup
removes their rows; for these four it also deletes their key-value storage
and their plugins/<id> folder, where sign-ins to bb's cloud live (owner
decision, 17.11.2026). A cloud plugin the user removed earlier keeps a row
with removedAt; those rows are purged the same way.

Desktop: without connect the app starts no account server sync, session
renewal or machine enrollment and opens no sign-in window, so the Server
menu has no "Sign in to bb Connect" item and nothing reaches getbb.app.
At start it deletes its stored connect machine credential and the bb
account cookie. The server target store forgets a saved connect server and
never chooses or adopts one. The account cookie goes on the default
account site and on the one behind the forgotten connect server. A server
that moved away through bb connect is not opened: the moved-server page
explains it and offers only Choose server.

The AI services text and search keyword no longer mention bb cloud.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
